WEBVTT

00:03.947 --> 00:05.863
I realize that you probably wouldn't know

00:05.946 --> 00:09.578
what to say to this,
but I want you to hear it.

00:11.547 --> 00:15.111
I guess I should start three years ago.

00:16.214 --> 00:18.812
Back when we still could've
changed something.

00:24.280 --> 00:27.597
Captain!
No word from the advance party.

00:27.681 --> 00:29.397
It's been two hours.

00:29.481 --> 00:31.862
Hmm.
Then have teams two and three

00:31.946 --> 00:33.397
prepare to land as well.

00:33.481 --> 00:34.663
Yes, sir!

00:34.747 --> 00:36.862
These damned island devils managed to

00:36.946 --> 00:39.463
defeat our Warrior unit.

00:39.547 --> 00:41.263
We need to find out
what they're doing now

00:41.347 --> 00:43.178
and relay it back to Marley.

00:47.347 --> 00:49.145
Grab onto something!

00:51.481 --> 00:54.545
It's... It's a devil!

01:09.880 --> 01:13.463
Hello, ladies and gentlemen of Marley!

01:13.547 --> 01:16.263
Welcome to Paradis Island!

01:16.347 --> 01:18.330
Nice to meet'cha. I'm Hange!

01:18.414 --> 01:20.531
And it's an honor to welcome
guests who've sailed from

01:20.615 --> 01:22.597
oh-so-far across the sea to come here!

01:22.681 --> 01:24.197
The trip must've left you exhausted,

01:24.281 --> 01:26.263
so why not join us for some tea?

01:26.347 --> 01:27.796
Oh! I almost forgot.

01:27.880 --> 01:29.663
If you were curious about
this guest of ours,

01:29.747 --> 01:30.663
he arrived just before you

01:30.747 --> 01:32.796
and we're already
getting along splendidly!

01:32.880 --> 01:36.378
Isn't that right? Tell them,
Nicolo!

01:37.547 --> 01:38.663
Please, Captain!

01:38.747 --> 01:42.463
Forget about me and gun these
devils down while you can!

01:42.547 --> 01:44.263
Huh? What are you saying?

01:44.347 --> 01:46.263
Captain!

01:46.347 --> 01:47.463
He's saying that he doesn't wanna be

01:47.547 --> 01:49.463
part of your shitty skit.

01:49.547 --> 01:50.796
Nicolo.

01:50.880 --> 01:52.863
Know this, you wretched devils!

01:52.947 --> 01:56.463
Marley doesn't negotiate
with filthy-bloods like you!

01:56.547 --> 01:58.263
And we're certainly not
gonna sit down with you

01:58.347 --> 02:00.263
and drink the pig piss you call tea!

02:00.347 --> 02:03.463
Huh?! Aw. Ya sure about that?

02:03.547 --> 02:05.263
Maybe you should be more polite.

02:05.347 --> 02:08.712
Unless you wanna piss off
the Titan looming behind you.

02:13.014 --> 02:15.731
Marley will never bend
to the power of devils!

02:15.814 --> 02:17.944
This is all she has to say to you!

02:24.746 --> 02:25.778
Huh?

02:31.746 --> 02:32.863
Put your hands up, Yelena!

02:32.947 --> 02:34.512
Lay down your weapons.

02:35.481 --> 02:36.463
What are you...?

02:36.547 --> 02:38.663
Do as she says.

02:38.746 --> 02:42.663
Hange. I'd like to
accept your invitation.

02:42.746 --> 02:44.278
Let's have some tea.

02:47.880 --> 02:52.877
How I've longed to meet you, Eren.

04:28.840 --> 04:30.822
That big lady shot and killed her captain

04:30.906 --> 04:33.357
without a second thought.

04:33.441 --> 04:35.357
What do you think she's hoping to do?

04:35.441 --> 04:38.090
Can't say, but even if she's on our side,

04:38.174 --> 04:39.822
we obviously can't trust her.

04:39.906 --> 04:41.557
No napping, Sasha.

04:41.641 --> 04:43.823
Yeah, but this is still
an incredible chance

04:43.907 --> 04:45.623
for us to gather information.

04:45.707 --> 04:47.623
We're really lucky we found them.

04:47.707 --> 04:50.037
You're right. We've been lucky.

04:50.840 --> 04:54.623
We managed to intercept
that ship by pure chance.

04:54.707 --> 04:58.623
If Marley comes to this island
in force, we're finished.

04:58.707 --> 05:00.472
We've gotta do something.

05:01.575 --> 05:05.023
Ohh? Ohh!

05:05.107 --> 05:06.557
Oh, I see now!

05:06.641 --> 05:09.423
So that's why your guns
can shoot so many bullets!

05:09.507 --> 05:12.438
Back in Marley, those weapons
are standard-issue.

05:13.575 --> 05:16.756
The Marleyan army is
comprised of 50 divisions,

05:16.840 --> 05:18.823
each made up of 20,000 troops.

05:18.907 --> 05:21.823
That comes out to a million
soldiers in total.

05:21.907 --> 05:23.557
Then there's the Marleyan navy.

05:23.641 --> 05:27.557
It's divided into three fleets,
with 21 battleships each.

05:27.641 --> 05:30.357
Marley's been developing
new weapons, too.

05:30.441 --> 05:33.357
They're making strides in
the field of aerial warfare.

05:33.441 --> 05:34.357
Aerial?

05:34.441 --> 05:38.756
Tch. Keep it together or
they'll think we're weak.

05:38.840 --> 05:39.956
I know that!

05:40.040 --> 05:42.823
In other words,
they're making flying ships,

05:42.907 --> 05:45.491
which can circumvent walls
by attacking from the sky.

05:45.575 --> 05:46.691
Huh?! They'll attack
from the sky?!

05:46.774 --> 05:48.756
Hange.

05:48.840 --> 05:51.557
If Marley truly has the
kind of military capabilities

05:51.641 --> 05:52.823
you just described to us,

05:52.907 --> 05:55.823
why haven't they sent an
invasion force in the past year?

05:55.907 --> 05:57.090
Tell me.

05:57.174 --> 06:00.357
There are two primary reasons.

06:00.441 --> 06:02.956
The first is the Pure Titans
Marley released here.

06:03.040 --> 06:05.357
They pose a serious threat
to a landing force,

06:05.441 --> 06:09.023
even if that force is armed
with the latest weaponry.

06:09.107 --> 06:11.557
They were originally taken
here to keep you Eldians

06:11.641 --> 06:14.956
confined within your walls,
but in more recent times,

06:15.040 --> 06:18.023
they've served as Eldia's
first line of defense.

06:18.107 --> 06:21.423
You don't say.
Well, isn't that funny?

06:21.507 --> 06:23.623
But it'll be morning shortly,

06:23.706 --> 06:26.357
and day is when Titans become active.

06:26.441 --> 06:28.023
Which tells me that if we're still here,

06:28.107 --> 06:31.023
sipping tea in the wilderness
beyond the walls,

06:31.107 --> 06:32.823
you must have killed all the Pure Titans

06:32.907 --> 06:34.738
that were roaming around.

06:36.507 --> 06:38.623
Is my assessment correct?

06:38.706 --> 06:40.423
And what if it is?

06:40.507 --> 06:42.771
You gonna take that intel back to Marley?

06:44.641 --> 06:46.823
Never. It's amazing.

06:46.907 --> 06:49.357
I am in awe.

06:49.441 --> 06:51.491
So what's the second reason?

06:51.575 --> 06:52.756
Marley is occupied.

06:52.840 --> 06:55.756
It's at war with an alliance
of several nations.

06:55.840 --> 06:58.957
It can't be bothered to
deal with Paradis now.

06:59.041 --> 07:02.090
You defeated the Warrior unit:
The pride of Marley.

07:02.174 --> 07:03.890
And in doing so, you stripped Marley of

07:03.974 --> 07:08.756
two of its best weapons:
The Colossal and Female Titans.

07:08.840 --> 07:11.023
Marley is a nation with many enemies.

07:11.107 --> 07:13.823
Once they saw that you'd
left it in a weakened state,

07:13.907 --> 07:16.957
they quickly joined
as one and declared war.

07:17.041 --> 07:19.690
I'm guessing that your group
infiltrated the Marleyan Army

07:19.774 --> 07:21.823
because you have some
sort of grudge against it.

07:21.907 --> 07:23.956
Are you undercover agents
from some of the nations

07:24.040 --> 07:25.771
that Marley's conquered?

07:27.040 --> 07:28.557
Oh? So I'm right!

07:28.640 --> 07:30.423
If you're willing to
go up against Marley,

07:30.507 --> 07:33.804
then you must be working with
some seriously powerful backers.

07:35.107 --> 07:35.956
Sorry to disappoint,

07:36.040 --> 07:39.622
but we're not agents
or anything of the sort.

07:39.706 --> 07:41.622
We were utterly powerless.

07:41.706 --> 07:46.423
Marley took our homes and
conscripted us into its army.

07:46.507 --> 07:47.956
The hope that we could
eventually strike back

07:48.040 --> 07:50.622
faded more every day.

07:50.706 --> 07:53.937
That is, until we met him.

07:55.107 --> 07:57.957
People feared that Titan the world over.

07:58.041 --> 08:00.491
They called him a devil.

08:00.575 --> 08:04.423
But to me, he looked like
something else entirely.

08:04.507 --> 08:05.756
A god.

08:05.840 --> 08:08.671
One that gave hope to the powerless.

08:12.574 --> 08:14.357
Our mutiny was carried out

08:14.441 --> 08:16.823
at the express command of Zeke Jaeger.

08:16.907 --> 08:19.957
We're the Anti-Marleyan Volunteers.

08:20.041 --> 08:23.838
And our goal is to
free the Eldian people.

08:25.574 --> 08:28.823
So, that concludes
Zeke Jaeger's requests.

08:28.907 --> 08:31.090
He claims that he can
save the Eldian people,

08:31.174 --> 08:32.690
who's existence is currently under th...

08:32.774 --> 08:33.556
Absurd!

08:33.640 --> 08:35.823
We shouldn't even be listening to this!

08:35.907 --> 08:37.756
We're talking about the Beast Titan here!

08:37.840 --> 08:39.556
He turned the people
of Ragako into Titans

08:39.640 --> 08:41.623
and spread terror within the walls!

08:41.707 --> 08:44.023
He hunted the Scouts to near-extinction!

08:44.107 --> 08:47.023
Now he has the gall to
come to us with requests?

08:47.107 --> 08:49.023
Zeke Jaeger's one and only goal is to

08:49.107 --> 08:51.756
steal the Founding Titan
from this island.

08:51.840 --> 08:54.423
He failed to by force,
so now he's trying to

08:54.507 --> 08:56.823
obtain it through diplomatic means.

08:56.907 --> 08:59.357
Yes, he should know
that we'll assume that.

08:59.441 --> 09:03.823
Regardless, I would still like
to hear what else he has to say.

09:03.907 --> 09:06.357
Zeke Jaeger claims to
have an actionable plan

09:06.441 --> 09:09.023
that can solve all our
people's problems at once.

09:09.107 --> 09:12.023
And to carry this plan out,
we would need two key assets:

09:12.107 --> 09:15.690
The Founding Titan, and a Titan
possessing royal blood.

09:15.774 --> 09:18.556
He says that with both,
the world can be saved.

09:18.640 --> 09:21.823
However, he will only reveal
the details of his plan

09:21.907 --> 09:24.623
after his conditions have been met.

09:24.707 --> 09:25.556
He's full of shit!

09:25.640 --> 09:28.623
What kind of feckless idiots
does he take us for?

09:28.707 --> 09:29.357
Eren?

09:29.441 --> 09:32.957
Zeke is telling
the truth. I remember.

09:33.041 --> 09:35.090
The Founder's power has always been

09:35.174 --> 09:38.357
completely impossible for me to use.

09:38.441 --> 09:39.756
The only exception was when I touched

09:39.840 --> 09:42.823
a Titan with royal blood.

09:42.907 --> 09:45.423
I recognize that Titan from a picture.

09:45.506 --> 09:49.090
It had to be my dad's
first wife. Dina Fritz.

09:49.174 --> 09:50.823
Zeke is Dina's son.

09:50.907 --> 09:52.823
He must have figured it out, too.

09:52.907 --> 09:56.357
How to get around the
king's vow renouncing war.

09:56.441 --> 09:57.690
How to activate the only hope

09:57.774 --> 10:00.490
that still remains to us Eldians.

10:00.574 --> 10:02.623
He knows how to wake
the millions of Titans

10:02.707 --> 10:04.423
sleeping in the walls.

10:04.506 --> 10:07.757
How to start The Rumbling,
and crush the world.

10:07.841 --> 10:13.357
Hey. Why did you keep
quiet about this for so long?

10:13.441 --> 10:16.423
'Cause I was concerned
for Historia's safety.

10:16.506 --> 10:19.023
At the time, I wasn't sure,
and I couldn't let her

10:19.107 --> 10:22.623
get turned into a Titan
based on some hunch of mine.

10:22.707 --> 10:25.490
It wasn't a well-thought-out
decision, I see that.

10:25.574 --> 10:27.423
We'll talk about it later.

10:27.506 --> 10:31.023
However, if everything
that you're saying is true,

10:31.107 --> 10:33.423
then Zeke's secret plan holds up.

10:33.506 --> 10:35.757
You trust them? Have you
lost your mind, Hange?

10:35.841 --> 10:37.757
The fact is, we can't risk letting these

10:37.841 --> 10:40.023
Marleyan soldiers roam the island freely.

10:40.107 --> 10:42.756
If we were smart, we'd hang them!

10:42.840 --> 10:45.357
No. That's not an option.

10:45.440 --> 10:48.957
If we want to protect Paradis
from Marley's survey ships,

10:49.041 --> 10:51.957
we need the volunteer's help.

10:52.041 --> 10:54.757
They have something
called a "radio."

10:54.841 --> 10:58.023
This is Survey Ship
One. Requesting immediate aid.

10:58.107 --> 11:01.423
This is Survey Ship One!
Please respond!

11:01.507 --> 11:03.423
We read you.
What's your situation?

11:03.507 --> 11:06.823
Thank goodness!
Our ship ran aground!

11:06.907 --> 11:09.357
We've been waiting so long for help.

11:09.440 --> 11:12.623
We're
coming! In the cove, huh?

11:12.707 --> 11:14.623
Our numbers? Don't worry!

11:14.707 --> 11:16.938
We're sending two survey ships your way.

11:18.375 --> 11:20.623
Hey! You all right?

11:20.707 --> 11:22.671
We're coming to pick you up!

11:25.574 --> 11:27.823
It's the Colossal Titan!

11:27.907 --> 11:29.005
How?!

11:29.640 --> 11:31.823
Hey! It's the enemy!

11:31.907 --> 11:33.357
Hurry! Jump off!

11:33.440 --> 11:34.556
Swim for the coast!

11:34.640 --> 11:35.971
Abandon ship!

11:41.107 --> 11:44.091
Welcome to our defiled island
of filth-blooded devils.

11:44.175 --> 11:45.957
You're gonna love it here.

11:46.041 --> 11:48.957
Long as you like drinking pig piss.

11:49.041 --> 11:50.757
Feel free to turn us down,

11:50.841 --> 11:52.823
but if you don't wanna come ashore,

11:52.907 --> 11:54.805
you'll need to swim back home.

11:56.374 --> 11:58.957
It was fun back then.

11:59.041 --> 12:01.023
We knew that as Eldians,

12:01.107 --> 12:04.023
we were feared and hated
by the rest of the world.

12:04.107 --> 12:06.423
By people on the other side of the sea

12:06.507 --> 12:08.838
whose faces we had never even seen.

12:09.707 --> 12:12.623
But not everyone across
the sea was an enemy.

12:12.707 --> 12:15.091
That fact gave us comfort.

12:15.175 --> 12:18.623
And we finally got to learn
about the outside world

12:18.707 --> 12:21.404
in all its complexities and mysteries.

12:22.774 --> 12:24.556
Oh, by the way.

12:24.640 --> 12:27.404
Why is your skin so dark, Onyonkopon?

12:28.507 --> 12:31.823
Because our creator thought that
things would be more interesting

12:31.907 --> 12:35.623
if the world were occupied
by many kinds of people.

12:35.707 --> 12:38.757
I'd say that applies to you
Subjects of Ymir as well.

12:38.841 --> 12:42.023
We exist because we were wanted.

12:42.107 --> 12:44.623
Wait, we were created? By who?

12:44.707 --> 12:47.957
By the one who gave power
to your Founder Ymir.

12:48.041 --> 12:49.838
It was God.

12:50.907 --> 12:53.091
Well, that's what some people believe.

12:53.175 --> 12:55.504
We're all free to think
as we like, right?

13:01.507 --> 13:03.757
What the hell is this food?

13:03.841 --> 13:05.690
Is it even edible?

13:05.774 --> 13:06.823
Smells pretty fishy.

13:06.907 --> 13:08.890
Have you never had seafood before?

13:08.974 --> 13:11.557
Nicolo's a master when it
comes to Marleyan cuisine.

13:11.641 --> 13:14.490
Dumb jerks. If you don't like
how it looks, then don't eat it.

13:14.574 --> 13:16.705
Like I care what Eldians think...

13:22.041 --> 13:23.023
It's so good!

13:23.107 --> 13:24.504
Slow down!

13:25.707 --> 13:26.823
No fair, Sasha!

13:26.907 --> 13:28.023
You're a genius.

13:28.107 --> 13:31.071
This is the best food I've ever eaten!

13:31.841 --> 13:34.690
Hey. Stop eating like
some kind of pig!

13:34.774 --> 13:37.571
I've never tasted anything like this!

13:39.041 --> 13:41.404
There's plenty, so take your time.

13:48.107 --> 13:50.757
We should be finished
building the port soon.

13:50.841 --> 13:52.423
Progress has been fast

13:52.507 --> 13:55.423
since those Marleyan engineers
decided to help out.

13:55.507 --> 13:57.504
I'm kind of surprised they agreed to.

13:58.641 --> 13:59.757
It took time.

13:59.841 --> 14:03.623
At first, we were too suspicious
to cooperate at anything.

14:03.707 --> 14:05.623
But as we gradually set aside the labels

14:05.707 --> 14:07.023
we have for one another,

14:07.107 --> 14:10.623
and work to see each other as people,

14:10.707 --> 14:12.705
we can reach an understanding.

14:14.374 --> 14:17.823
Armin. Have you seen any
of Bertholdt's memories?

14:17.907 --> 14:22.891
Uh... yeah, but I didn't notice
anything that seemed helpful.

14:22.975 --> 14:24.823
We're short on time.

14:24.907 --> 14:27.891
Zeke has less than three years to live.

14:27.975 --> 14:30.490
Yeah, but about that.

14:30.574 --> 14:31.957
Do you really think it's okay for us

14:32.041 --> 14:34.891
to just go along with Yelena's plan?

14:34.975 --> 14:36.690
What's the problem?

14:36.774 --> 14:38.423
I just wonder if we really have to

14:38.507 --> 14:40.023
threaten the world with the Rumbling

14:40.107 --> 14:42.423
to protect the Eldian people.

14:42.507 --> 14:44.557
We'd be forcing everyone
to live in fear of us.

14:44.641 --> 14:47.371
Acting like the devils they think we are.

14:48.107 --> 14:51.356
Before it comes to that,
why don't we just talk to them?

14:51.440 --> 14:53.957
If we fix the world's
misconceptions about us,

14:54.041 --> 14:55.623
threats won't be needed.

14:55.707 --> 14:59.423
Come again? What
misconceptions do they have?

14:59.507 --> 15:01.823
You know. How they think
we're scary monsters.

15:01.907 --> 15:03.957
They think that because we can transform

15:04.041 --> 15:06.023
into man-eating Titans.

15:06.107 --> 15:08.271
That's no "misconception."

15:09.307 --> 15:12.423
But still. There are
some Marleyans who like us.

15:12.507 --> 15:13.957
How many?

15:14.041 --> 15:16.356
Most of the Marleyans we caught
are still glaring at us

15:16.440 --> 15:18.423
from their prison cells.

15:18.507 --> 15:20.957
That's true for now,
but given enough time.

15:21.041 --> 15:24.638
Yeah. We just need time.

15:25.507 --> 15:28.690
That's right, and to
buy ourselves that time,

15:28.774 --> 15:31.705
we need to show the world our strength.

15:37.507 --> 15:39.356
I still don't know

15:39.440 --> 15:42.238
that we made the right choice back then.

15:44.174 --> 15:46.891
I can't help but wonder if there was

15:46.975 --> 15:51.271
some other path we could've
taken, if we'd just seen it.

15:52.507 --> 15:54.023
I used to think

15:54.107 --> 15:56.823
that I understood Eren
better than anyone.

15:56.907 --> 15:58.757
Even Mikasa.

15:58.841 --> 16:02.438
But... I don't know anymore.

16:16.907 --> 16:19.423
Hey! Aren't you a Marleyan?

16:19.507 --> 16:21.090
What the hell are you doing?

16:21.174 --> 16:24.090
This graveyard is full of
people your kind killed!

16:24.174 --> 16:25.023
You have no right...

16:25.106 --> 16:26.023
Hey, stop!

16:26.106 --> 16:28.271
Let us take care of this guy!

16:29.440 --> 16:31.823
I'm sorry, but please.

16:31.907 --> 16:34.557
Marleyans can go to hell.

16:34.641 --> 16:35.623
Hey, Nicolo!

16:35.707 --> 16:37.557
You okay?

16:37.641 --> 16:40.304
No. Why, damn it?

16:41.841 --> 16:44.271
Is it true that Sasha was killed?

16:45.507 --> 16:48.490
So it is. Then why?

16:48.574 --> 16:50.838
What the hell were you guys doing?

16:55.441 --> 16:58.757
Shot by a kid who snuck onto the airship?

16:58.841 --> 17:02.471
It's too ridiculous to be true.

17:03.641 --> 17:08.357
It wasn't an ordinary kid.
The girl had been trained.

17:08.441 --> 17:10.557
Sounds like a Warrior candidate.

17:10.641 --> 17:13.605
Should've kept my
guard up. I'm sorry.

17:14.641 --> 17:17.423
Why apologize to me?

17:17.507 --> 17:19.838
All I did was cook her a meal or two.

17:21.574 --> 17:23.356
Thank you.

17:23.440 --> 17:27.671
Thank you for every tasty meal
you made for her, Nicolo.

17:29.040 --> 17:31.905
How are you taking it, Conny?

17:32.975 --> 17:36.371
Sasha and I were like twins.

17:37.841 --> 17:40.838
So it feels like half of me is just gone.

17:43.707 --> 17:45.557
It's her family.

17:45.641 --> 17:48.772
Y'all were friends
with my daughter, Sasha?

17:56.707 --> 17:58.757
Uh. Pardon.

17:58.841 --> 18:00.023
I'm just a captive Marleyan,

18:00.107 --> 18:03.438
but I have permission to work as a chef.

18:04.841 --> 18:06.757
Your daughter loved my cooking

18:06.841 --> 18:09.757
more than anyone else ever will, I think.

18:09.841 --> 18:13.757
So um, if you ever want to,

18:13.841 --> 18:16.471
please come and let me
cook you something.

18:21.641 --> 18:23.557
This would be on the house, right?

18:23.641 --> 18:25.705
Yeah.

18:33.507 --> 18:36.423
How interesting.
They're calling it a victory?

18:36.507 --> 18:39.557
Ignorance is scary,
but delusion's even worse.

18:39.641 --> 18:42.623
I'm going to kill you and
ship your corpse back to Marley,

18:42.707 --> 18:45.357
with a note about your little plot.

18:45.441 --> 18:47.956
Should spell the end
for your grandparents.

18:48.040 --> 18:51.423
That said, if this secret plan
of yours isn't bullshit,

18:51.507 --> 18:54.423
I can wait and chop you up
once it's finished.

18:54.507 --> 18:56.956
I don't care much either way.

18:57.040 --> 19:00.357
Well, I appreciate your
willingness to accommodate.

19:00.441 --> 19:03.956
But hey. I do get to
meet Eren soon, don't I?

19:04.040 --> 19:05.956
There's no need to rush.

19:06.040 --> 19:08.891
We've prepared a nice little
place for you to stay here.

19:08.974 --> 19:12.238
A beautiful hotel that you can relax at.

19:15.040 --> 19:19.357
So, could I ask you to stop glaring?

19:19.441 --> 19:21.423
This is all the Titan
transformation serum

19:21.507 --> 19:23.956
we were able to steal from Marley.

19:24.040 --> 19:27.090
Sorry, but it's hard to reproduce.

19:27.174 --> 19:31.423
It's fine. For our
purposes, this should be plenty.

19:31.507 --> 19:33.423
I just wish that we were in a position

19:33.507 --> 19:35.490
to return your kindness.

19:35.574 --> 19:37.423
We owe you so much already.

19:37.507 --> 19:41.023
You turned our ignorance into
hope and got nothing in return.

19:41.107 --> 19:43.557
For us to doubt the people who saved us,

19:43.641 --> 19:46.423
we truly are no better than devils.

19:46.507 --> 19:49.423
It is my opinion that
we've proven ourselves

19:49.507 --> 19:52.623
to be your loyal friends
over these past three years.

19:52.707 --> 19:54.623
This is a shame.

19:54.707 --> 19:56.890
The weapons that we offered you as gifts

19:56.974 --> 20:00.623
were intended to bring freedom
to the Eldian people.

20:00.707 --> 20:03.357
I know that this is a selfish request,

20:03.441 --> 20:06.557
but would you please overlook
our weakness for a time?

20:06.641 --> 20:10.823
We're going to great lengths
to keep Zeke on a tight leash.

20:10.906 --> 20:13.890
It's fine, Commander.
I understand.

20:13.974 --> 20:15.023
The day will soon come when we

20:15.107 --> 20:17.438
sit at the same table once again.

20:19.441 --> 20:21.956
This is my hotel?

20:22.040 --> 20:24.757
What better lodging could there be?

20:24.840 --> 20:26.823
It's a giant forest.

20:26.906 --> 20:29.956
Difficult to move through
and devoid of boulders.

20:30.040 --> 20:33.757
Looks like a fun spot
for using ODM gear, too.

20:33.840 --> 20:35.490
Hey. Quick question.

20:35.574 --> 20:36.557
This natural wonder.

20:36.641 --> 20:39.757
Would you mind letting me
show it to Gabi and Falco?

20:39.840 --> 20:45.772
Tch. Whether they get to see the
sights or not depends on you.

20:53.907 --> 20:57.956
I'll kill you, Eren Jaeger.

20:58.040 --> 21:00.623
Eren was ready to do it alone.

21:00.707 --> 21:03.823
Whether we helped him or abandoned him.

21:03.907 --> 21:06.638
The outcome would've
been awful either way.

21:07.575 --> 21:11.557
But now, we've killed
a huge number of people.

21:11.641 --> 21:15.423
Sailors. Soldiers. Civilians.

21:15.507 --> 21:20.090
The devastation we spread
was indiscriminate.

21:20.174 --> 21:23.822
Still, if we had left that port intact,

21:23.906 --> 21:26.023
then Marley would've launched
an immediate counterattack

21:26.107 --> 21:28.491
against our island.

21:28.575 --> 21:30.822
We've abandoned all hope for peace,

21:30.906 --> 21:34.423
but we didn't have a choice.

21:34.507 --> 21:37.305
Any more than the three of you did.

21:38.707 --> 21:41.890
Right, Annie?

21:41.974 --> 21:44.771
Say something. Please.

21:47.974 --> 21:49.956
Kill or be killed.

21:50.040 --> 21:52.738
Fight for your life.

22:00.507 --> 22:03.557
The only way to live is to fight.

22:03.641 --> 22:07.004
So fight. Just fight.

23:40.632 --> 23:43.414
Without any allies on the outside,

23:43.498 --> 23:46.881
they must kill their
enemies in order to live.

23:46.965 --> 23:49.614
But is that the right choice to make?

23:49.697 --> 23:52.348
There isn't a soul who knows.

23:52.432 --> 23:54.995
Next episode:
"A Sound Argument."
